{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_h4_via_pachner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_h4_via_pachner","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L89-L94","doc":"**Consequence (sorry-free given the class).** The conjectural Pachner→h⁴\nidentification: the state-sum h⁴ coefficient equals the Borromean\nMarkov-trace `−3/4` (division-free form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_decompositions_agree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_decompositions_agree","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L80-L87","doc":"**Consequence (sorry-free given the class).** The 2-octahedron and\n8-tetrahedron Borromean decompositions yield the SAME Φ_q state sum —\ntriangulation-independence of the Borromean invariant, derived from\nPachner invariance + their 2–3-relatedness.  This is the content the\nGemini \"flips compose to the identity\" picture refers to, made precise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.four_h4_eq_neg_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.four_h4_eq_neg_three","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L75-L75","doc":"**CONJECTURAL** identification with the Borromean Markov-trace coefficient\n(`tr_M(β_Bor) = 1 − (3/4)·h⁴ − …`, `BorromeanMarkovTrace`), written\ndivision-free as `4·coeff = −3`.  UN-EXHIBITED — this field is the §3b\nconjectural content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.h4_stateSum_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.h4_stateSum_coeff","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The `h⁴` coefficient extracted from the Pachner-invariant state sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_pachner_related","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borromean_pachner_related","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L68-L68","doc":"The two Borromean decompositions are related by Pachner moves (class field). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borTetrahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borTetrahedral","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Its 8-ideal-tetrahedron subdivision (four tetrahedra per octahedron). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borOctahedral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.borOctahedral","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L64-L64","doc":"The decomposition of `S³ ∖ 𝓑₃` into two regular ideal octahedra (Thurston). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.pachner_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.pachner_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L62-L62","doc":"**Pachner 2–3 invariance** — STANDARD given the Φ_q pentagon: the state\nsum is constant on 2–3-related triangulations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.PachnerRelated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.PachnerRelated","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Pachner 2–3 relatedness of two triangulations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.stateSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.stateSum","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The Turaev–Viro / Reshetikhin–Turaev Φ_q state sum on a triangulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.Tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.Tri","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Abstract ideal triangulations of `S³ ∖ 𝓑₃`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean.mk","kind":"ctor","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PachnerPentagonBorromean","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/PachnerPentagonBorromean.lean#L45-L75","doc":"**conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean (D15)** as a §3b conjecture-class over a\ngeneric value ring `R` (the state-sum / coefficient ring).\n\nAn instance is a CONJECTURAL WITNESS — the categorical `(u,v)`\nspecialisation that makes the Pachner-invariant Φ_q state-sum h⁴\ncoefficient equal the Borromean Markov-trace `−3/4`.  The natural-\nspecialisation probe currently exhibits NO such witness (see header), so\nno instance is provided. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean","label":"conj:pachner-pentagon-borromean","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/pachner-pentagon-borromean.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}